pm8916-bms-vm: use the vendor vbat LSB (293 uV, not 300)

The BMS reports the battery through a 1/3 divider at 97656 uV per bit, so
one LSB is 97656 / 1000 * 3 = 292.97 uV.  The downstream qpnp-vm-bms
driver converts exactly that way and the OCV table in the board DTS was
measured against it, but mainline used 300 uV -- 2.4 % high, which shifts
every capacity point down by roughly nine percentage points at 85 %.

Measured on mifib-v12 (pack at rest, charger held off): the gauge read
4.299 V against 4.184 V at the battery connector, i.e. ~292 uV/LSB.  It
also made a healthy full pack report "Over voltage" (4.33 V against a
4.2 V design maximum).

Introduce PM8916_BMS_VM_VBAT_LSB_UV and use it for the FIFO sample, the
probe-time OCV and the resume OCV.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/pm8916_bms_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pm8916_bms_vm.c
@@ -41,6 +41,19 @@
 #define PM8916_BMS_VM_DATA_CTL2 0x43
 #define PM8916_BMS_VM_FIFO_CNT_SD_CLR BIT(2)
 
+/*
+ * Vbat LSB.  The BMS reports the battery through a 1/3 divider at
+ * 97656 uV per bit, i.e. 97656 / 1000 * 3 = 292.97 uV per LSB.  The
+ * downstream qpnp-vm-bms driver uses exactly that (V_PER_BIT_MUL_FACTOR
+ * 97656 / V_PER_BIT_DIV_FACTOR 1000, then VBATT_MUL_FACTOR 3), and the
+ * OCV table in the board DTS was measured against it -- so the two have
+ * to agree or every capacity point is shifted.  Mainline used 300, which
+ * reads 2.4 % high: a full 4.2 V pack showed up as 4.33 V (and tripped
+ * the over-voltage health flag).  Measured on mifib-v12: gauge 4.299 V
+ * vs 4.184 V at the connector, i.e. ~293 uV/LSB.
+ */
+#define PM8916_BMS_VM_VBAT_LSB_UV 293
+
 /* Using only 1 fifo is broken in hardware */
 #define PM8916_BMS_VM_FIFO_COUNT 2 /* 2 .. 8 */
 
@@ -239,7 +252,7 @@
 	 * Just use the last measured value for now to report the current
 	 * battery voltage.
 	 */
-	bat->vbat_now = vbat_data[PM8916_BMS_VM_FIFO_COUNT - 1] * 300;
+	bat->vbat_now = vbat_data[PM8916_BMS_VM_FIFO_COUNT - 1] * PM8916_BMS_VM_VBAT_LSB_UV;
 
 	/*
 	 * Release the FIFO latch.  FIFO_CNT_SD stays set until it is
@@ -329,7 +342,7 @@
 		goto comm_error;
 
 	bat->last_ocv_time = ktime_get_seconds();
-	bat->last_ocv = tmp * 300;
+	bat->last_ocv = tmp * PM8916_BMS_VM_VBAT_LSB_UV;
 	bat->vbat_now = bat->last_ocv;
 
 	pm8916_bms_vm_update_temp(bat);
@@ -399,7 +412,7 @@
 			       bat->reg + PM8916_BMS_VM_S3_S7_OCV_DATA0, &tmp, 2);
 
 	bat->last_ocv_time = ktime_get_seconds();
-	bat->last_ocv = tmp * 300;
+	bat->last_ocv = tmp * PM8916_BMS_VM_VBAT_LSB_UV;
 
 	ret = regmap_write(bat->regmap,
 			   bat->reg + PM8916_SEC_ACCESS, PM8916_SEC_MAGIC);
